course: dictionary
lesson: 14601
title: One word, three meanings: poaching
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. You can find the right one by reading the words around it. Look for clues such as animals, eggs or players. «Poaching» is a good example, because it has three different meanings.
explain: «The rangers caught two men poaching rhinos in the park.» Rhinos are animals, and the men are hunting them secretly and against the law, so poaching means catching animals illegally. «Dad is poaching eggs for breakfast.» The clues are eggs and breakfast, so here poaching means cooking gently in water.
explain: «The big club was accused of poaching players from its rivals.» A club does not hunt players, so poaching here means taking people away from someone else. Always ask what the sentence is about, then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Poaching means hunting or catching animals, birds or fish illegally, often on someone else's land.
fact: Poaching can also mean cooking an egg or fish gently in water or milk that is just below boiling.
fact: Poaching can mean taking someone else's workers, players or ideas, as in «poaching players».
fact: Rangers work to stop poachers, who hunt elephants and rhinos for their ivory and horns.
fact: When a word has more than one meaning, use the other words in the sentence to choose the right one.
exercise: «The rangers arrested the poaching gang in the forest.» What does poaching mean here? | *Hunting animals illegally | Walking very quietly | Cooking food slowly in water | Taking players from another team
exercise: «Mum poached two eggs gently in a pan of water.» What does poached mean here? | Broken into a bowl | *Cooked gently just below boiling | Fried very fast in hot oil | Thrown away because they were bad
exercise: «The club was accused of poaching a talented young player.» What does poaching mean here? | Practising football in the rain | *Taking someone else's player away | Watching the game from the stands
test: Which sentence uses poaching to mean taking someone else's players? | «Poaching gives a soft, tasty egg.» | «Poaching is against the law in this national park.» | *«The club tried poaching the best striker from its rival.»
test: What do you put in the pan when you are poaching eggs? | *Water or milk just below boiling | Oil | Ice | Sugar
exam: Which meaning of poaching fits «Ravi was poaching ideas from the shop next door»? | *Taking someone else's ideas or workers | Hunting animals illegally | Cooking gently in water
